2. Find the lowest point on the terrain and use that as the starting point for the river.
3. Create a path for the river by randomly selecting a direction to move in and then moving in that direction while also adding some randomness to the path. You can use a combination of Perlin noise and a random number generator to achieve this. 
4. As the river flows, adjust the height of the terrain around it to create banks that follow the curves and bends of the river.
5. Vary the width and depth of the river by adjusting the height of the terrain around it. You can use a combination of Perlin noise and a random number generator to achieve this as well.
6. Once the river has reached the edge of the terrain, you can either stop it or continue it by wrapping it around to the other side of the terrain.
